&lt;p data-renderer-start-pos=&quot;662&quot;&gt;Any information you submit to Datadog as part of your application will be processed in accordance with Datadog’s&amp;nbsp;&lt;a class=&quot;c-link&quot; href=&quot;https://www.datadoghq.com/legal/applicant-candidate-privacy/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; data-stringify-link=&quot;https://www.datadoghq.com/legal/applicant-candidate-privacy/&quot; data-sk=&quot;tooltip_parent&quot;&gt;Applicant and Candidate Privacy Notice&lt;/a&gt;. For information on our AI policy, please visit &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.datadoghq.com/legal/interviewing-at-datadog-ai-guidelines/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Interviewing at Datadog AI Guidelines&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://www.relexsolutions.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/01/relex-greenhouse-banner-top.png&quot; alt=&quot;&quot; width=&quot;1280&quot; style=&quot;max-width: 100%;&quot;&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Every RELEX implementation is a solution built from scratch for one customer: their processes, their data, their targets. (Senior) Supply Chain Consultants shape both sides of that build — the business processes and KPIs the customer will run on, and the configuration that makes them work in the system. Depending on your background you will lean more towards one side than the other. This is a heavily customer-facing role.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll be doing&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Understand how the customer really plans.&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Prepare, facilitate and document workshops to gather and specify business requirements, and run the data analysis that shows where the strengths and the gaps actually are.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Design the target picture&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;— planning processes, roles and the KPIs the project is measured on — and guide customers towards RELEX best practice, including where their current way of working needs to change.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Build it.&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Configuration, business rules, workflows and reporting that deliver the design you just agreed, and that hold up in operation: nightly run performance, scalability and maintainability, not just functional correctness.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Make the value case tangible&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;for customer leadership: define how forecast accuracy, availability, inventory and cost will be measured, and report honestly on where we stand.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Take it live.&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Coordinate User Acceptance Testing, resolve what testing surfaces, and upskill super users so the customer is proficient and self-sustaining after go-live.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Own adoption, not just delivery.&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;A technically correct solution that nobody uses is not a successful project.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Document what you built&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;— requirements, scope and configuration — so the project team, the customer and our Continuous Services colleagues can work with it after handover.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Work across disciplines&lt;/strong&gt;: with Technical Consultants on the data model, interfaces and the customer&#39;s ERP landscape, and with Project Managers on scope, effort and timelines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Within RELEX&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Challenge and develop implementation best practice across industries (grocery, DIY, home goods, pharma, wholesale and more)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Share knowledge with the team as both a trainer and a participant, and support colleagues who are earlier in their journey&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with our global teams on international projects and bring practices between regions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use AI tooling actively in your daily work — we expect curiosity here and give you room to experiment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What we&#39;re looking for&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Around 2+ years of relevant experience&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;in supply chain or retail planning, demand and inventory planning, or in implementing / consulting on planning software. A degree in supply chain management, business, engineering, mathematics or computer science is a good foundation — but we care more about what you have actually done.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Structured thinking and comfort with ambiguity.&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Many customer requirements arrive without a ready-made answer. You break them down, work with data, and arrive at a defensible recommendation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Communication that works across levels&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;— from super users in a training room to senior stakeholders in a steering committee, including the conversations where the message is not what the customer hoped to hear.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Business-fluent German and English.&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Both are used daily.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Willingness to travel&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;depending on the project phase.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Technical affinity&lt;/strong&gt;: SQL, scripting, or an interest to pick these up&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Additionally, for the Senior level:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Several years of consulting or implementation experience, including&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;demonstrable ownership of a workstream or a smaller project end-to-end&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;— scope, risk, timeline and completion, not just your own tasks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Reliable effort estimation for standard and custom requirements, supporting scoping and SOW discussions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience coaching and mentoring less experienced colleagues&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Confidence in front of senior customer stakeholders, including steering committees&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience with a supply chain planning system, either as a user or as an implementer&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience defining and tracking KPIs or building a value case&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Who we are&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;We’re bold thinkers and kind teammates, growing fast but staying grounded. Our Nordic roots and global outlook shape a culture of friendliness, creativity, and collaboration, all powered by openness and shared wins. We care deeply about doing the right thing - and doing it together.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul class=&quot;p-rich_text_list p-rich_text_list__bullet p-rich_text_list--nested&quot; data-stringify-type=&quot;unordered-list&quot; data-list-tree=&quot;true&quot; data-indent=&quot;0&quot; data-border=&quot;0&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Flexibility in how and where you work&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Room to thrive&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;in a fast-growing global company with a good market position&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Practical benefits that support work, family, wellness, and everyday life&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Annual leave&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Diverse, inclusive, and supportive work culture&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work that meaningfully reduces waste and improves sustainability&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ownership, autonomy and flat hierarchies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Two paid volunteering days each year&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;We are a global community of different cultures, voices, and experiences. We celebrate what makes us unique and connect through what we share, in an authentic and safe environment. Together we shape the future, and each other.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;If you feel this is the opportunity you don’t want to miss, you can apply by sending your resume through the application form as soon as possible. Please note that we cannot process any applications through email.   &amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong data-stringify-type=&quot;bold&quot;&gt;Apply today and be part of the future. Be RELEX!&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://www.relexsolutions.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/01/relex-greenhouse-banner-bottom.jpg&quot; alt=&quot;&quot; width=&quot;1280&quot; style=&quot;max-width: 100%;&quot;&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Associate Director / Director, Data Strategy &amp;amp; Measurement&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Location: Remote&lt;/em&gt; — this is a remote, work-from-home role, as are all positions at Acceleration Partners. Some travel is required for client meetings, internal meetings, conferences, and industry events.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Role &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Associate Director / Director, Data Strategy &amp;amp; Measurement is responsible for defining and leading Acceleration Partners&#39; data, analytics and measurement capability. This role sits at the intersection of client strategy, data science, measurement, AI-enabled insights and commercial growth. The Director will work directly with enterprise clients to understand their marketing and business data ecosystem, develop measurement strategies, and help clients make better decisions through data. Internally, the role will partner with Client Services, Strategy, Sales and AI Automation teams to build AP&#39;s data capability, improve decision-making, develop new services and products, and raise data literacy across the organization. As a senior leader, the Director will also develop AP&#39;s market position as a leading authority on affiliate, influencer and partnership measurement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Top Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Client Measurement &amp;amp; Data Strategy&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Serve as AP&#39;s senior advisor on measurement, analytics and reporting.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Understand client data ecosystems including affiliate networks, influencer platforms, Google Analytics, CRM systems, customer databases, MMM outputs and business intelligence tools.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Design measurement frameworks that connect partnership marketing activity to broader business outcomes, spanning attribution, incrementality, customer acquisition and lifetime value.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Advise clients on how affiliate and influencer activity should be measured alongside paid media, brand marketing and broader customer acquisition strategies.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Own AP&#39;s point of view on measurement, partnering with MMM providers, analytics platforms and measurement vendors to keep AP at the forefront of measurement innovation.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strategic Consulting &amp;amp; Problem Solving&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Lead analytical workstreams for enterprise clients, including programme audits and strategic reviews.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Support growth strategies, forecasting, partner valuation models and opportunity assessments.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Translate complex datasets into actionable commercial recommendations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Partner with senior client stakeholders across Marketing, Analytics, Finance and Data Science teams.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Data Products &amp;amp; Capability Development • Define and own AP&#39;s data and analytics roadmap.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Partner with Strategy and AI teams to identify opportunities for automation and AI-enabled insights.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Lead development of scalable reporting frameworks, dashboards, benchmarking products and measurement tools.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Drive innovation across APVision and future analytical capabilities.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Data Enablement &amp;amp; Industry Thought Leadership&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Increase data literacy across Account Management, Strategy and Sales teams through training programmes, workshops and playbooks.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Coach teams to ask better questions, interpret data effectively and communicate insights to clients.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Represent AP externally as a thought leader on measurement and analytics, speaking at conferences, webinars and client forums.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Produce thought leadership on attribution, incrementality, MMM, AI and partnership measurement, and build relationships with key industry vendors and platforms.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What Success Looks Like:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;By 6 Months&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Director has built strong relationships with key enterprise client stakeholders and is actively advising on measurement strategy and programme audits. They have an established working relationship with their Data Strategist and a clear view of AP&#39;s data and analytics roadmap. Early training and enablement sessions have begun to raise data literacy across Account Management and Strategy teams.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;By 1 Year&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Director is recognized internally and externally as AP&#39;s leading voice on measurement and analytics. Clients are adopting AP&#39;s measurement recommendations, and client satisfaction and retention have improved. The Director has contributed to new business wins, launched at least one new analytical product or framework, and represented AP at industry events. Data literacy and standardized analytical frameworks are visible across the organization, and the Data Strategist is developing well under their mentorship.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualities of the Ideal Candidate:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Strategic thinker, comfortable operating with ambiguity&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Strong communicator and storyteller, able to simplify complex concepts for non-technical audiences&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Commercially minded&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Collaborative and influential across teams and seniority levels&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Naturally curious and innovative&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Confident representing AP as an external thought leader&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum Qualifications &amp;amp; Skills:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• 8–12+ years of experience in analytics, measurement, marketing science, consulting or data strategy&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Experience working with enterprise clients and advising senior stakeholders and executive teams&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Strong understanding of affiliate, influencer, digital marketing or performance marketing&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Experience leading teams and developing talent&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Strong understanding of Marketing Mix Modelling (MMM), attribution methodologies and incrementality testing&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Proficiency with Google Analytics, Customer Data Platforms (CDPs) and Business Intelligence/dashboarding tools (Tableau, Power BI, Looker or similar)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Familiarity with data warehousing concepts and AI-enabled analytics&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• SQL and data querying experience preferred&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WHY ACCELERATION PARTNERS?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Acceleration Partners is the world’s largest and first-to-market Partnership and Marketing Agency creating and nurturing partnerships that drive exceptional measurable outcomes for their clients. Managing clients in 40+ countries, their global team of 300+ focuses on data-driven strategies that help connect brands to the right consumers through performance partnerships, traditional affiliate, influencer, performance PR, content and B2B partnership marketing. Serving over 200 brands with household names like Amazon, Target, Google, Warby Parker, Crocs, Reebok (to name a few) their diversified staff is creating what’s next in the industry by building balanced portfolios of high-performing partnerships. As the only truly integrated global partnerships agency, Acceleration Partners prides themselves on being on the cutting edge of new industry developments, and leveraging their proven expertise to bring unique solutions to the most complex challenges for brands who aim for growth.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;AP PERKS &amp;amp; BENEFITS – WHAT WE OFFER&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;100% remote work for everyone&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Group medical, dental, and vision coverage insurance (with opt-out benefits)&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;401K with matching&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Open Paid Time Off&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Summer &amp;amp; Holiday Wellness Breaks in July and December&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Volunteer and Birthday Time Off&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Focus Fridays&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Paid Parental Leave Benefits&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Wellness, Technology &amp;amp; Education Allowances&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Paid sabbatical leaves, donation matching, and more!!&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Target base salary is £65K - £85K depending on location and experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Benefits may vary based on employment status or country location.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Acceleration Partners is committed to a diverse workforce and we are an equal opportunity employer. We evaluate applicants regardless of an individual&#39;s age, race, color, gender, religion, national origin, sexual orientation, disability, or veteran status.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
